 kit flow - shows where the work stands, from backlog to releases

   one of
   *kit flow*                   shows where the work stands, from backlog to releases

     --no-fetch   --fresh     fetches nothing; incoming says so

     --text   --json   --jq   prints the picture as text, even on a terminal

     one of
     --all                    every issue and pull request (the default); it stands alone
     --mine --others --owner

     --workspace              draws each stage across a workspace's members with checkouts, a
                              group's name or a repository's host and path, as kit workspaces names
                              it; see Over a workspace

   --stages                   prints the stages the picture draws, one per line, in order
   --me                       prints the caller's login on the primary's forge, the login --mine and
                              --others match
   --quota                    prints the caller's rate limits on the primary's forge, as one JSON
                              array: each forge's {forge, limits}, each limit {name, limit,
                              remaining, reset}; reading them costs a request at most
   --marks                    prints a mark per stage, as one JSON object, which changes when what
                              the stage draws does: read again, a mark that differs says the stage
                              is stale; on GitHub, nothing changed costs no request
   backlog                    the open issues not closed by any open pull request, oldest first;
                              underway has the rest
   underway                   the open issues closed by an open pull request: who works on each, and
                              where
   incoming                   what fetching every remote brought: default-branch commits, branches
                              new and gone
   desk                       the root checkout: branch, ahead and behind, uncommitted paths
   worktrees                  every linked worktree: branch, ahead and behind, uncommitted paths
   changes                    the open pull requests, each with the issues it closes
   builds                     the runs not owned by any pull request: the default branch, tags,
                              schedules
   releases                   the releases on the forge, newest first
   repos                      the repositories of the workspace, or the one here: each one's forge,
                              remotes, checkout, and its desk's branch


 kit flow
